  "status": "Appeal Received",
  "description": "We propose to replace all existing timber windows, with uPVC windows of the exact same design and size as the existing. ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed uPVC windows, by reason of their materials and detailed design,&amp;nbsp; are unsympathetic and out of keeping with the original building, resulting in an&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;overly regular, plainer appearance, with much thicker and more obtrusive glazing bars, &lt;/span&gt;resulting in unacceptable harm to the character and appearance of the subject property and the terrace it forms part of. As such, the proposed development is contrary to policies D1 (London’s form, character and capacity for growth) and D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) D4 (Good design) and HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) of the London Plan (2021), policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP4 (Non-designated Heritage Assets) and LP17 (Housing Design) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020) and Hackney&#x27;s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2009).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
